    consequence: "The Disc III Black Mage Village Weapon Shop listings (Bandana, Chain Plate, Leather Plate, and Mythril Vest) and Daguerreo Weapon Shop listings (Asura's Rod, Hamelin, Octagon Rod, Obelisk, Rune Blade, Tiger Fangs, and Diamond Armor) are replaced by different Disc IV weapon stock. Oeilvert, Desert Palace, and Esto Gaza become inaccessible after the Shimmering Island transition. The original PlayStation Item Location Guide lists earlier shop routes for Bandana and pickup, steal, and shop routes for Chain Plate, Leather Plate, and Mythril Vest; the reviewed Disc IV shop tables omit these items, and no later acquisition route for the four appears in the reviewed references. Missing all listed routes can therefore leave the item types without a documented recovery, but this remains source-limited rather than direct proof that no other route exists.",
    deadline: "Before travelling to Shimmering Island at the end of Disc III.",
    nextAvailability: "Black Mage Village and Daguerreo remain visitable, but their weapon inventories have changed; Oeilvert, Desert Palace, and Esto Gaza are no longer accessible. The reviewed original PlayStation shop and item-location references list no later Bandana, Chain Plate, Leather Plate, or Mythril Vest acquisition, while the broader item and ability catalog remains partial. Bandana and Mythril Vest are consumed by the Silk Robe and Brave Suit recipes respectively, so retain one of each if those syntheses are part of your goal.",
    action: "Use the final shop list in Preparing to Leave to compare your inventory with the equipment and abilities you actually want, especially the four Black Mage Village and seven Daguerreo weapon listings that leave those shops after the transition. GameFAQs gives quantity targets for an endgame inventory route; subtract pieces already spent in synthesis and do not treat those counts as a universal minimum. If you plan to synthesize Silk Robe or Brave Suit, reserve one Bandana or Mythril Vest for the recipe.",
    recovery: "For Bandana, Chain Plate, Leather Plate, and Mythril Vest, collect the copies your goal needs before their final documented sources close: the Disc III Black Mage Village listings are the last listed BMV routes, and Esto Gaza's Mythril Vest stock closes with the Shimmering Island transition. The reviewed Disc III–IV Treno, Lindblum, and Alexandria stock tables and Disc IV Black Mage Village list no later purchase route for these items. This item-type risk is source-limited pending direct game verification, not a claim that every possible release or route has been checked. Other stock items still need individual recovery review.",
    note: "The original PlayStation Item Location Guide lists Bandana's earlier shops and notes no Find/Win/Steal source, while the newer GameFAQs walkthrough/item reference separately documents a Dragon's Gate pickup. It also enumerates the listed earlier pickups, steals, and shops for Chain Plate, Leather Plate, and Mythril Vest. GameFAQs Shops shows the changed Disc IV Black Mage Village weapon stock and omits all four; its Disc III–IV Treno, Lindblum, and Alexandria lists also omit Bandana. Bandana and Mythril Vest are consumed by Silk Robe and Brave Suit respectively, so players pursuing those syntheses should reserve a copy. GameFAQs lists source shops, purchase counts, and selected abilities; Jegged, GameFAQs, and EliteGrindLab differ on which Disc III equipment is a final ability source. The guide preserves that conflict and keeps the complete ability-source audit partial.",
