    action: "Complete the full transition sweep before following Mikoto through the green gate: collect Coronet and Dragon Wrist from Terra's hidden fork; take the Terra-path Elixir, Remedy, Mythril Racket, and Demon's Vest; then follow the hidden route after the bridge to the Minerva's Plate chest. At Bran Bal, take Flash Hat, both local Elixirs (the laboratory basement and Inn), Wing Edge, and Angel Earrings. Minerva's Plate is described as Terra or Bran Bal depending on the source; follow the chest route once rather than counting duplicate copies.",
    recovery: "The later route returns through Bran Bal only as part of a linear story sequence, then gathers the Genomes and escapes on the Invincible; no reviewed source confirms a free return to the earlier pickup rooms or Moorock's shop. If a selected goal tracks exact location copies, reload a save from before the green gate. Item types remain recoverable: Daguerreo sells the six listed equipment types, while Elixir, Remedy, Wing Edge, and Angel Earrings have separate item paths. Rank S is a 340-point threshold, about 75% of the game's treasures, not a full-sweep requirement.",
    note: "GameFAQs and Jegged describe a linear post-Kuja story passage back through Bran Bal, with Zidane and Dagger gathering the Genomes before the escape aboard the Invincible. The Terra/Bran Bal labels for Minerva's Plate differ: GameFAQs and Jegged list it under Terra, while EliteGrindLab files the same hidden stairway chest under Bran Bal; the GameFAQs item-location index lists both headings, but the reviewed route sources do not establish two distinct chest copies. GameFAQs lists seven route pickups under Terra, while EliteGrindLab groups the Minerva chest under Bran Bal. GameFAQs's Bran Bal item index also includes Stiltzkin's Diamond/Ether/Elixir bundle; this warning separately counts the two room Elixirs. The route models one Minerva chest and the two local Bran Bal Elixirs; the conservative pre-gate checkpoint remains, and no permanent item-type loss is inferred. The rank formula assigns one point per qualifying chest, hidden field icon, or event-sequence item; see the linked sources for the full categories and 340-point threshold.",
